      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{8-10\\cos(x)}{3}=-\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot \\cos(x)+\\frac{8}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\cos(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-\\frac{10}{3}.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=|-\\frac{10}{3}|=\\frac{10}{3}.$",
